{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and actuation as separate plants, then encode a compact supervisor policy with specification automata that map sensed obstacle conditions to one-shot motion choices. The policy prioritizes move_forward in clear space, allows occasional random_walk for coverage variation, uses directed turns for side/front obstacles, uses move_backward only in dedicated front-recovery, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-front-blocked last-resort path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability",
    "Use one-shot action states so open-loop pulses complete without being preempted by path_clear",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward forward progress with only occasional random_walk",
    "Route obstacle_front through backward-then-turn recovery, with a rare stuck path to full_rotate",
    "Keep obstacle_left and obstacle_right recovery directional and consistent"
  ],
